00:47:23,520 --> 00:47:28,140
Scott: It's like a surreal-y, jovially haunted video poker.

558
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:28,481
Scott: Yeah.

559
00:47:28,762 --> 00:47:34,637
Rym: Like imagine you died and you went to Purgatory, but Purgatory has video poker and they're like, look, this isn't heaven.

560
00:47:34,998 --> 00:47:35,680
Rym: This isn't hell.

561
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:38,388
Scott: It's more like a slightly twisted, but not dark.

562
00:47:38,449 --> 00:47:41,280
Scott: It's like a brightly lit fun house video poker.

563
00:47:41,380 --> 00:47:41,561
Scott: Yeah.

564
00:47:41,801 --> 00:47:42,363
Rym: A fun house.

565
00:47:42,383 --> 00:47:48,020
Rym: that's not going to kill you, but might unerve you a little bit, but it definitely trapped you.

566
00:47:48,780 --> 00:47:51,199
Scott: It's sort of laughing at you and also with you.

567
00:47:51,460 --> 00:47:51,701
Scott: Yep.

568
00:47:53,624 --> 00:48:01,479
Rym: The other thing I really appreciate about it is that one, you can click to see your deck at any time and it helpfully counts cards for you.

569
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:03,602
Rym: Just so you don't have to worry about that.

570
00:48:04,925 --> 00:48:13,800
Rym: But two, like Slay the Spire and unlike Cobalt Core, it lets itself be insanely unbalanced.

571
00:48:14,060 --> 00:48:16,540
Rym: Like there are combos you can pull off just like in Slay the Spire.

572
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:17,145
Scott: That's the point.

573
00:48:17,185 --> 00:48:18,980
Scott: You have to be unbalanced or otherwise you're not going to win.

574
00:48:19,160 --> 00:48:19,401
Scott: Yeah.

575
00:48:19,621 --> 00:48:21,165
Rym: But also like that's fun.

576
00:48:21,245 --> 00:48:21,926
Rym: Slay the Spire.

577
00:48:21,967 --> 00:48:26,717
Rym: Part of the why it's fun is sometimes, yeah, I got 4,000 poison on that boss.

578
00:48:26,777 --> 00:48:28,020
Rym: Wasn't that fun to pull off?

579
00:48:28,120 --> 00:48:31,247
Rym: Or yes, I literally got an infinite combo until the boss died.

580
00:48:31,607 --> 00:48:32,810
Rym: This game can do the same thing.

581
00:48:32,870 --> 00:48:37,500
Rym: Well, I can only get Royal Flushes with a 50 X multiplier every time.

582
00:48:39,481 --> 00:48:46,260
Scott: The other thing is that much like Slay the Spire where the, you know, the enemies have like these unique abilities that might counteract your strategy.

583
00:48:46,560 --> 00:48:53,340
Scott: Like, you know, you go all in on doing lots of tiny attacks and then that certain Slay the Spire boss, I forget which one because it's been a while.

584
00:48:53,820 --> 00:48:54,783
Rym: Timeboy is the worst.

585
00:48:54,803 --> 00:48:58,134
Rym: Like, yeah, I can play shivs for hours.

586
00:48:58,234 --> 00:49:00,901
Rym: And then Timeboy is like, no, you're playing 12.

587
00:49:00,901 --> 00:49:01,364
Scott: That's right.

588
00:49:01,405 --> 00:49:02,412
Scott: That's the one I'm talking about.

589
00:49:02,452 --> 00:49:02,814
Rym: Hate him.

590
00:49:02,855 --> 00:49:03,519
Rym: He's the worst one.

591
00:49:04,160 --> 00:49:04,602
Scott: That's what I was.

592
00:49:04,642 --> 00:49:04,782
Scott: Yeah.

593
00:49:04,823 --> 00:49:05,425
Scott: That's what I was thinking.

594
00:49:05,445 --> 00:49:05,726
Rym: Well, I care.

595
00:49:05,746 --> 00:49:10,220
Scott: What's the whole, Latro will do the same thing where it's like, ah, yes, I see you have made an amazing deck.

596
00:49:10,320 --> 00:49:12,485
Scott: Well, uh, guess what?

597
00:49:13,387 --> 00:49:15,532
Scott: All of these cards have been debuffed.

598
00:49:15,732 --> 00:49:19,180
Rym: The one, the one that attacks heart specifically got me in my first play through.

599
00:49:19,280 --> 00:49:23,874
Rym: Cause first, first, my first like ground up to the boss, I like double down on hearts.

600
00:49:23,914 --> 00:49:26,040
Rym: I made this like heart specific deck and it was so good.

601
00:49:26,401 --> 00:49:29,470
Rym: And the next time I see at the end, the boss is like, hearts are debuffed.

602
00:49:29,510 --> 00:49:32,700
Rym: And I was like, oh, I guess the powers won't work, but maybe the cards will work.

603
00:49:32,780 --> 00:49:35,366
Rym: Now debuff is way worse than you think it is in this game.

604
00:49:36,027 --> 00:49:36,287
Scott: Yeah.

605
00:49:36,568 --> 00:49:37,670
Scott: It makes the card do nothing.

606
00:49:37,771 --> 00:49:42,280
Scott: Um, so there are a few things in the UI that weren't obvious in case anyone out there plays.

607
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:44,729
Scott: There's probably more things that I haven't even discovered yet.

608
00:49:45,070 --> 00:49:47,719
Scott: Um, but these are things I discovered that are really fascinating one.

609
00:49:48,841 --> 00:49:49,041
Scott: Yeah.

610
00:49:49,081 --> 00:49:52,492
Scott: You can, there's two buttons to sort your hand by rank or by suit.

611
00:49:52,612 --> 00:49:55,020
Scott: And that's, you know, you're going to use those most often.

612
00:49:55,682 --> 00:49:58,990
Scott: You can just rearrange your hand any way you want by clicking and dragging.

613
00:49:59,391 --> 00:50:02,960
Scott: So that's, you know, might useful in some certain circumstances.

614
00:50:03,940 --> 00:50:16,880
Scott: Um, also, uh, sometimes there'll be things, usually bosses that make your hand have cards that are phased out, but you can actually see in the animation, which cards are moving where.

615
00:50:17,761 --> 00:50:21,146
Scott: Um, and you know, that when you sort by suit and rank, right?

616
00:50:21,186 --> 00:50:22,649
Scott: What order the suits are in.

617
00:50:23,510 --> 00:50:30,180
Scott: And so you can actually deduce when you buy flipping between the rank, the rank sorting and the suit sorting.

618
00:50:30,780 --> 00:50:35,029
Scott: And like, which cards must be like, Hey, that car is on the far right.

619
00:50:35,129 --> 00:50:36,692
Scott: And I sorted by rank and suit.

620
00:50:36,753 --> 00:50:38,015
Scott: And that car didn't move.

621
00:50:38,376 --> 00:50:39,879
Scott: It must be this suit.

622
00:50:40,701 --> 00:50:44,226
Scott: And it must be a really low rank because it's all the way on the right.

623
00:50:44,286 --> 00:50:53,080
Scott: And it's still there, but no matter which sorting I choose, you can sort of figure out which cards are, which, um, what suits they belong to and things of that nature.

624
00:50:53,840 --> 00:50:55,023
Scott: The tarot cards.

625
00:50:55,945 --> 00:51:02,819
Scott: A lot of times, some of the tarot cards force you to select cards in your hand to get used on.

626
00:51:02,839 --> 00:51:03,340
Scott: Right?

627
00:51:03,741 --> 00:51:09,229
Scott: So when you in the shop and you buy a tarot card, it makes you like use it immediately.

628
00:51:09,289 --> 00:51:15,720
Scott: If you get it from a booster pack and it'll basically draw a whole bunch of cards from your deck randomly for you to use it on.

629
00:51:16,200 --> 00:51:18,430
Rym: Which could fuck you over depending on what you picked.

630
00:51:18,450 --> 00:51:20,580
Scott: If you get a bad draw, you can always, you can always skip.

631
00:51:20,741 --> 00:51:21,002
Scott: True.

632
00:51:21,042 --> 00:51:24,280
Rym: But then he wasted the money and money's hard to come by.

633
00:51:24,840 --> 00:51:26,022
Scott: It's easy to get a lot of money.

634
00:51:26,242 --> 00:51:36,020
Scott: And in fact, it's sort of a problem sometimes and you get too much money because you did, you invested in money and now your deck doesn't score any points yet cash out your money.

635
00:51:36,641 --> 00:51:50,660
Scott: Um, and it's also, it took me a few runs to realize, wait a minute, when I get a pile of money, I should reroll and blow it all in the shop and reroll to get lots and lots of bonuses and not just buy what's in the shop and click next and keep my money.

636
00:51:51,301 --> 00:51:51,882
Rym: Not even expense.

637
00:51:51,922 --> 00:51:52,663
Rym: What, like five bucks?

638
00:51:53,505 --> 00:51:55,488
Scott: The reroll as you use the reroll.

639
00:51:55,689 --> 00:52:01,880
Scott: every time you reroll it, the price goes up, but there are things you can get obviously to decrease the cost of the reroll.

640
00:52:02,601 --> 00:52:16,320
Scott: So, but anyway, the another trick I learned is that, so you have sometimes there'll be a tarot card just like in your inventory and you'll be like, well, I guess I have to wait to use that until I'm actually like playing and I have a hand to use it on.

641
00:52:16,841 --> 00:52:26,960
Scott: But actually if you buy a tarot card pack that draws out a bunch of random cards, you can actually use the tarot card in your inventory on those cards.

642
00:52:28,580 --> 00:52:33,587
Scott: So you don't have to wait until like you're in a game looking at a hand of cards, right?

643
00:52:34,228 --> 00:52:42,900
Scott: But you may want to cause some tarot cards are like turn three cards into clubs and it's like, well, I'll just wait until I've got two clubs and now I got a flush.

644
00:52:44,081 --> 00:52:50,574
Scott: And that might be better than using it in advance and hoping you just increase your chance of drawing a bunch of clubs, right?

645
00:52:50,654 --> 00:52:53,600
Scott: Guarantee that you have five clubs at some point.

646
00:52:54,544 --> 00:52:56,958
Scott: And then from that point forward, it's the same either way.

647
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:17,700
Scott: The negative thing I can say about this game is that being a very much beginner at it and not knowing all the things I need to know and not being highly skilled and knowing the best strats and whatnot is that it seems like most of the best strats involve getting particular combinations of jokers and getting them early.

648
00:53:18,261 --> 00:53:23,220
Scott: And the jokers are just way more powerful than the other things in the game or more significant and important.

649
00:53:23,481 --> 00:53:29,160
Rym: Yeah, because they're permanent powers that often do things like the multiplier is just better by a lot.

650
00:53:29,880 --> 00:53:29,980
Scott: Yeah.

651
00:53:30,020 --> 00:53:35,086
Scott: So all the times I've won were with particularly powerful joker combinations.

652
00:53:35,507 --> 00:53:46,360
Scott: And so it's like I feel like my strategy right now, still being a beginner, is get money, use that money to dig and find a powerful joker combination and then coast.

653
00:53:46,600 --> 00:53:48,586
Rym: Well, I mean, Slay the Spire is the same thing.

654
00:53:48,646 --> 00:53:53,800
Rym: Like once you like, I know every card in Slay the Spire now, so I can sort out those combos.

655
00:53:53,920 --> 00:54:00,260
Rym: But sometimes like you're going to do well if you get the thing that reduces any damage less than five or less to one.

656
00:54:00,621 --> 00:54:06,520
Rym: And you also get the thing that reduces all damage by one, thus reducing anything five or less to zero.

657
00:54:07,261 --> 00:54:09,307
Scott: Yeah, but I do feel like that can't be there.

658
00:54:09,408 --> 00:54:13,100
Scott: I feel like there is other ways to win that I'm just not good enough and haven't discovered yet.

659
00:54:14,823 --> 00:54:15,999
Scott: So I'm working on that.

660
00:54:16,120 --> 00:54:19,034
Rym: Yeah, but it's I mean, it's this is worth fifteen bucks.

661
00:54:19,094 --> 00:54:20,280
Rym: It's very well designed.

662
00:54:20,440 --> 00:54:21,451
Scott: It was I bought it on sale.

663
00:54:21,471 --> 00:54:22,199
Scott: I think it was less than that.

664
00:54:22,521 --> 00:54:24,330
Rym: I think I bought it on sale too.

665
00:54:25,195 --> 00:54:26,179
Rym: It's fifteen bucks right now.

666
00:54:26,400 --> 00:54:27,062
Scott: It wasn't a big sale.

667
00:54:27,082 --> 00:54:27,965
Scott: It was a small sale.

668
00:54:28,005 --> 00:54:30,091
Scott: But this is a million seller.

669
00:54:30,613 --> 00:54:31,756
Scott: And I spoke.

670
00:54:31,817 --> 00:54:32,940
Scott: I have spoken to people.

671
00:54:33,640 --> 00:54:40,360
Scott: I spoke to people at PAX and a couple other people who were not the kind of person who you think would play a game like this.

672
00:54:40,500 --> 00:54:43,952
Scott: But they got hooked on it because I guess, you know, it's a lot of Twitch people playing it.

673
00:54:44,073 --> 00:54:45,959
Scott: Other people see it and they play it.

674
00:54:46,881 --> 00:54:51,740
Rym: And, you know, and I will say if you like this game, you'll probably like Slay the Spire 2 and vice versa.

675
00:54:52,620 --> 00:54:54,584
Scott: Yeah, they're all they're all in the same category.

676
00:54:54,664 --> 00:55:02,840
Scott: And I think while on the one hand, you know, you might want to criticize people for just sort of going ham on this sort of card based roguelike deal.

677
00:55:04,701 --> 00:55:06,244
Scott: I think it's perfectly OK.

678
00:55:06,505 --> 00:55:06,665
Scott: Right.

679
00:55:06,705 --> 00:55:07,326
Scott: It's like how many.

680
00:55:07,707 --> 00:55:14,218
Scott: there's a lot less card based roguelikes than there are platformers or FPS or RTS or RPGs.

681
00:55:16,020 --> 00:55:16,481
Scott: Right.

682
00:55:16,501 --> 00:55:24,621
Scott: So but also they could use a lot more of these that are a lot of deck builder was invented in 2008.

683
00:55:24,621 --> 00:55:27,720
Rym: So it's a deck builder itself is a brand new genre.

684
00:55:28,641 --> 00:55:29,523
Scott: Yeah, there's a lot.

685
00:55:29,563 --> 00:55:32,932
Scott: I think there's still a lot more space to be explored with these kind of games.

686
00:55:33,133 --> 00:55:35,860
Scott: And I'm excited every time there's another good one.

687
00:55:37,181 --> 00:55:42,598
Scott: I think I might even preliminarily say this could be like the second best one yet.

688
00:55:43,561 --> 00:55:53,600
Rym: I could see that because while Cobalt Core has a lot going for it and specific mechanics in it, I think are better than the games it was based on as a game.

689
00:55:53,700 --> 00:55:55,719
Rym: It definitely runs out of strategic chapter real quick.

690
00:55:56,261 --> 00:56:02,960
Scott: I think that's the number one factor I judge these games based on is like, how long can you hold your interest?

691
00:56:03,320 --> 00:56:03,420
Scott: Right.

692
00:56:03,441 --> 00:56:07,420
Scott: Because it's like a roguelike could drop your interest after like a single play.

693
00:56:07,861 --> 00:56:07,981
Scott: Right.

694
00:56:08,343 --> 00:56:12,880
Scott: Because all you know that all you're going to be doing is whatever you just did after your first run.

695
00:56:13,442 --> 00:56:15,999
Scott: You know that you're just going to be doing that a lot more.

696
00:56:16,522 --> 00:56:17,649
Scott: Nothing else is going to happen.

697
00:56:17,669 --> 00:56:19,200
Scott: There isn't going to be anything else in the game.

698
00:56:19,641 --> 00:56:21,526
Scott: So if you don't enjoy that, you're not going to enjoy it.

699
00:56:21,626 --> 00:56:27,040
Scott: So if you're doing a lot of runs, then that means it's an enjoy, right?

700
00:56:27,661 --> 00:56:30,000
Scott: It's just how many can you do before you get tired of it?

701
00:56:30,380 --> 00:56:31,869
Scott: How much juice can you squeeze?

702
00:56:32,009 --> 00:56:33,820
Scott: Because all the juice is going to be the same flavor.

703
00:56:34,040 --> 00:56:38,051
Rym: Seven years later, I'm still squeezing that Slay the Fire juice like at least once a week.

704
00:56:38,091 --> 00:56:40,017
Rym: I'll just do a quick run like while I'm laying in bed.

705
00:56:40,719 --> 00:56:41,080
Rym: No biggie.

706
00:56:47,170 --> 00:56:49,459
Rym: This has been GeekNights with Rym and Scott.

707
00:56:49,520 --> 00:56:52,050
Rym: Special thanks to DJ Pretzel for the opening theme.

708
